nging the total risk very little we  could have avoided a lot of economic  destruction  now that is me still manning a left-wing  case against lockdowns  do i literally believe it one hundred  percent of course not of course not  one example lots of younger people live  with older people  so if you want to keep the young  restaurant worker employed  but their grandparents safe and they  live together  how do you do it right so it it doesn't  literally work  in all cases but i want to hear your  thoughts and the point  that i'm making is left-wing skepticism  of a total and complete stay at home is  okay  the right-wing skepticism and attacks  on the guidelines are ridiculous and  they're wrong  and they're laughable there is a  sensible conversation to have about how  it could have been handled differently  and it may be relevant  for when wave two happens if we have a  break between wave one and wave two  but we've got to actually think it  through and that's what i'm trying to do  with you right here  let me know what you think i'm on  twitter at dpakman remember we have a  daily hour podcast that you can get on  itunes  stitcher google play and all of your  favorite podcast  apps make sure to sign up for it and let  me know your thoughts  on twitter where i am at deepakman  one of our sponsors nordvpn is giving  you  70 off a three-year plan which comes out  to just a little over three bucks a  month  and you'll get an extra month free when  you go to nordvpn.com  david pakman or just go to their site  and use the coupon code  david pakman it's 2020. there is really  no reason  not to be using a vpn not using a vpn  means  you are not taking your internet safety  seriously i use nordvpn  almost anytime i'm using the internet it  hides your ip address when you're  browsing online keeps you safe from  hackers  keeps websites from tracking your  browsing activity  many advantages and nordvpn is the most  trusted vpn  in the game they don't log your internet  activit